// PauseRelayWithBodyWithResponse Pause the relay (optionally a single bucket)
//
// Each relay instance re-reads the desired state on its own control-refresh tick (the relay's reclaimInterval, 5s by default), so the effect lags by up to that interval - it is not immediate, and a worker mid-dispatch finishes what it already claimed. When a bucket is paused, its owning worker keeps renewing the bucket's lease and simply stops dispatching sends for it; pause never releases the lease (use POST /relay/buckets/{bucket}/release for that). Pausing a single bucket requires LEASE coordination and returns 409 otherwise - see the bucket field on BucketSelector.
